      "AUCUOTA PAULIE LERNIN\nMID-WEEK PICTORTAL\nPUBLISHED WEEKLY BY THE NEW YORK TIMES COMPANY\nVOL. XLI, NO. 11\nWE DO OUR PART\nAPRIL 27, 1935\nPRICE TEN CENTS\nTHE START OF A 2,400-MILE FLIGHT\nOVER THE PACIFIC\nThe nineteen-ton Pan American Clipper\nflying over the piers of the San Francisco-\nOakland bridge on the hop which took it\nfrom Alameda, Calif., to Pearl Harbor,\nHawaii, in 17 hours 45 minutes.\n(International.)",
      "August Pailie Lot:\nMID-WEEK PICTORIAL\nPUBLISHED WEEKLY BY THE NEW YORK TIMES COMPANY\nVOL. XI, NO. 18\nDECEMBER 14, 1935\nPRICE TEN CENTS\nMANILA WELCOMES THE FIRST TRANSPACIFIC AIR MAIL\nThe China Clipper descending to the harbor in the Philippine capital after making the 8,000-mile crossing from the\nCalifornia coast in 59 hours 47 minutes actual flying time. This photograph was brought to America\nby the Clipper on its return voyage.\n(Times\nWide World Photos)"
